# x1-validator-private-rpc: every 2 hours, on the hour, check that nginx's
# list holds at least one api key, and send a Telegram alert while it holds
# none, since nginx then refuses every request.
# apply installs this line for you, with apiKeyCountCheckHours in place of
# the 2. To install it by hand, as the validator's account, run crontab -e
# and paste the line below. It makes the logs/ folder its output goes to,
# when it's missing.
0 */2 * * * mkdir -m 755 $HOME/x1-validator-services/x1-validator-private-rpc/logs 2>/dev/null; $HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.X.Y/bin/node $HOME/x1-validator-services/x1-validator-private-rpc/src/cli.js ensure-there-is-at-least-one-rpc-api-key --quiet >> $HOME/x1-validator-services/x1-validator-private-rpc/logs/ensure.log 2>&1
